# Typography (TY)

This is the short form. Before writing code in this area, read the full rules with reasons, bad/good examples and checks: `.ui-polish/rules/03-typography.md`.

- **TY-01 A real typeface is configured** (error). The project loads a specific typeface for body text (and optionally a second for headings) and exposes it as `--font-sans` / `--font-display` / `--font-mono` tokens. Do not leave the browser default, and do not ship a bare system stack unless `design.md` says the system font is the brand choice (then set `"allowSystemFonts": true` in `ui-polish.config.json`).
- **TY-02 The font is chosen for this product, not by habit** (warning). Use the fonts named in `design.md`. If the brand has none, pick a pairing from the table below that matches the product's personality, and record it in `design.md` with one sentence of reasoning. Inter, Roboto, Poppins, Open Sans, Montserrat, Lato, Space Grotesk and Geist are allowed only when `design.md` names them as the brand's decision.
- **TY-03 Fonts load without invisible text or layout shift** (warning). Load fonts with `next/font`, or self-host WOFF2 with `font-display: swap`, or a Google Fonts `<link>` with `&display=swap` plus `<link rel="preconnect">`. Request only the weights used (normally 400, 500, 600 or 700; variable fonts where available). Give the fallback stack a metric-compatible fallback so the swap does not reflow the page.
- **TY-04 One `<h1>`, no skipped heading levels** (warning). Each page has exactly one `<h1>` naming the page. Sections use `<h2>`, subsections `<h3>`, in order, without skipping. Choose the level for document structure and the size with a class; a small heading is still an `<h2>` if it starts a section.
- **TY-05 A real type scale with few sizes** (warning). Use one scale and at most about eight sizes across the product. A workable app scale: 12, 14, 16, 18, 20, 24, 30, 36px (`text-xs` to `text-4xl`); marketing pages may add 48 and 60. Body text is 16px (14px only in dense tables and secondary UI, never below 12px). Each step up the hierarchy changes size by a visible ratio (1.2 or more) or changes weight; never both size and weight and colour for one small step.
- **TY-06 Line height and line length are set for reading** (warning). Body text has line-height 1.5 to 1.7; headings 1.1 to 1.25 (tighter as size grows); UI labels and buttons 1.2 to 1.4. Paragraphs are 45 to 75 characters wide: constrain text blocks with `max-w-prose` (65ch), never let paragraphs span a 1200px container. Use `text-wrap: balance` on headings and `text-wrap: pretty` on paragraphs.
- **TY-07 Numbers are tabular and formatted** (warning). Anywhere digits line up or change (tables, prices, stats, timers, counters, pagination) use `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`. Right-align numeric columns. Format with `Intl.NumberFormat` and `Intl.DateTimeFormat` (thousands separators, currency, units, locale dates), never by string concatenation.
- **TY-08 Weight, tracking and case are used sparingly** (info). Use two or three weights (400 body, 500 or 600 for emphasis and UI, 600 or 700 for headings). Tighten letter-spacing slightly on large headings (-0.01 to -0.03em); add 0.04 to 0.08em only on small all-caps labels. All caps is for labels of one to three words, never sentences. Do not use light (300) weights below 20px or grey text lighter than `--muted-foreground` for content.
